#!/usr/bin/python3
# q2headtrack - head rotation (3DoF) for SteamVR on the Quest 2: reads the SyncBoss IMU (~1 kHz accel + gyro),
# fuses it into an orientation and publishes it in /dev/shm/q2pose for the q2hmd SteamVR driver.
#   q2headtrack            run (as root; started by q2vrtest)
#   q2headtrack recenter   make the current direction "forward"            (Ctrl+Alt+C)
#   q2headtrack next       try the next IMU axis orientation (24)         (Ctrl+Alt+R)
# The IMU mounting is fixed (see DEFAULT below); gravity at start only sets the initial tilt, and the direction
# you face at start is "forward".
# Fusion: gyro integration (bias measured while still) + slow tilt correction from the accelerometer; no
# magnetometer, so yaw drifts slowly - recenter fixes it.  Log lines "q2-head: ...".
# Credit: the SyncBoss IMU details and the gyro-bias tracking (re-estimate after 1 s still, small step) follow
# nicolas-riera/quest1-steamos (Quest 1 SteamOS port, src/monado/.../quest1_hmd.c, docs/syncboss-imu.md), used with
# the author's permission.
