#!/bin/bash
# q2vrbench (desk-294) - one unattended comparison: Steam drawing its VR panels at the headset rate (steamMatchesHMDFramerate)
# or not, now that Steam has real GPU sync (desk-293) and SteamVR has its own cores (desk-290).  Panel rate from the layer log.
# Runs once (until /var/lib/q2/bench291.done exists; /var/lib/q2/nobench = never).  For each variant: restart Steam
# with it (/tmp/q2bench.env, read by /tmp/q2steam-run.sh and the steamwebhelper wrapper), let it settle, open the big
# dashboard (q2vrdash, /tmp/q2dashreq), measure 30 s, close it, measure 15 s.  Measured: CPU of Steam's web UI (and its
# compositor thread), of Steam, of vrcompositor; SteamVR's frame timing (compositor GPU ms, dropped frames); temperature;
# whether the web UI's GPU process restarted.  Result: /var/log/q2/vrbench.txt (goes out with Ctrl+Alt+U).
